<article class="env-lemma" id="0BHC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BHC">Lemma <span data-tag="0BHC">89.3.2</span>.</a> Let $X, x_ i, U_ i \to X, u_ i$ be as in (<a href="/tag/0BHA" data-tag="0BHA">89.3.0.1</a>). If $f : Y \to X$ corresponds to $g_ i : Y_ i \to U_ i$ under $F$, then $f$ is quasi-compact, quasi-separated, separated, locally of finite presentation, of finite presentation, locally of finite type, of finite type, proper, integral, finite, if and only if $g_ i$ is so for $i = 1, \ldots , n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Limits of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BGZ" data-tag="0BGZ">70.19.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>